Find the limits: 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\lim_{x \to 1} [x^3 - x^2 + 1]$
    \item $\lim_{x \to 3} [x(x + 1)]$
    \item $\lim_{x \to -1} [1 + x + x^2 + \ldots + x^{10}]$
\end{enumerate}

pert_a:
 The required limits are all limits of some \textcolor{red}{rational} functions. Hence the limits are the values of the function at the prescribed points. We have:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\lim_{x \to 1} [x^3 - x^2 + 1] = 1^3 - 1^2 + 1 = 1$
    \item $\lim_{x \to 3} [x(x + 1)] = 3(3 + 1) = 3(4) = 12$
    \item $\lim_{x \to -1} [1 + x + x^2 + \ldots + x^{10}] = 1 + (-1) + (-1)^2 + \ldots + (-1)^{10} = 1 - 1 + 1 - 1 + \ldots + 1 = 1$
\end{enumerate}

